<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Knight in the Panther's Skin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1200</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Knight in the Panther's Skin is a Georgian epic poem written by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shota-rustaveli">Shota Rustaveli</a> around 1200 and dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar</a>. It tells of the knights Avtandil and Tariel and their quest for Tariel's lost beloved, Nestan-Darejan, celebrating friendship, loyalty and love. It is regarded as the national epic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-knight-in-the-panthers-skin.jpg" alt="The Knight in the Panther's Skin" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 三猎 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E3%80%8A%E8%99%8E%E7%9A%AE%E6%AD%A6%E5%A3%AB%E3%80%8B%E6%8A%84%E6%9C%AC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
